# --- Secrets / local launcher (contains an API key — never commit) ---
claude-ds.sh
.env
.env.*

# --- Claude Code local state ---
.claude/
.claude.local.md

# --- Vendored reference repos (read-only, fetched via scripts) ---
references/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Triton / CUDA build + cache artifacts ---
.triton/
*.ptx
*.cubin
*.ttir
*.ttgir
*.llir

# --- Profiler output (Nsight Compute / Systems) ---
*.ncu-rep
*.nsys-rep
*.qdrep
*.sqlite

# --- Benchmark scratch ---
bench_out/
*.csv
*.png
.vscode/

# --- Toolchain installers pulled down during setup, never part of the repo ---
*.deb
*.run

# Triton perf_report writes this stub beside its plot; the plots go to
# results/, which is already ignored, but a stray run can drop one here.
results.html

# --- Local scratch notes, not part of the repo ---
REMOTE.md

# --- Benchmark output ---
#
# Ignored by default: a results/ directory is per-machine, and a laptop run and
# an A100 run write the same filenames. But the docs cite specific files as the
# evidence behind published numbers, and evidence that is not in the repo is
# not evidence -- a fresh clone was getting six broken references. So the
# measurements and figures that docs/ points at are un-ignored individually.
#
# The line is drawn at *what a number came from*, not at *what a run produced*:
# the sweep CSVs, the per-pass CSVs, the figures and the measurement logs stay;
# the 350 KB compiler transcripts from building flash-attn and bootstrapping the
# box do not. Those prove a build happened, which no document claims.
#
# Two ordering rules make this work, and each one silently broke it once:
#
# 1. `results/*`, not `results/`. Git never descends into an excluded
#    *directory*, so a negation under one can never match -- it is dead text.
#    Excluding the contents lets git look inside and test each entry.
# 2. This block sits at the end of the file. The last matching pattern wins,
#    and `*.csv` / `*.png` under "Benchmark scratch" above would otherwise
#    re-ignore every figure and measurement un-ignored here.
results/*
!results/*.csv
!results/*.png
!results/a100-device.txt
!results/a100-sweep.log
!results/a100-twopass.log
!results/a100-pass2.log
!results/a100-roofline.log
!results/a100-dip-stages.log
!results/a100-dip-overhead.log
